From: SPOTTER <deployment/flowsint-patches>
Subject: [PATCH] Bind the Flowsint app UI to loopback instead of 0.0.0.0

Upstream publishes the Flowsint SPA as a bare "5173:8080", which Docker binds on
0.0.0.0. That made it the one genuinely LAN-reachable service in the stack, and
it is UNAUTHENTICATED in the sense that matters here: SPOTTER's access control is
an nginx auth_request gate in front of it, which a direct connection to 5173
walks straight past. Anyone on the same network reached the investigation UI, and
with it the graph, with no login.

SPOTTER serves this UI through its authenticating gate on http://localhost:8082.
The direct port stays bound to 127.0.0.1 as a break-glass path.

This cannot be fixed with a compose override: compose APPENDS to the `ports`
list rather than replacing it, so an overlay would leave the 0.0.0.0 binding in
place alongside the new one. The upstream file has to be patched.

Apply with:  git -C "$FLOWSINT_HOME" apply <this file>
scripts/bootstrap.sh does it, and scripts/preflight_env_check.py fails if 5173
is bound to anything but loopback -- that check is the backstop if this is ever
skipped or lost to an upstream update.

diff --git a/docker-compose.prod.yml b/docker-compose.prod.yml
index 9027a99..884bd6c 100644
--- a/docker-compose.prod.yml
+++ b/docker-compose.prod.yml
@@ -147,8 +147,12 @@ services:
     container_name: flowsint-app-prod
     restart: always
     ports:
-      # The only network-facing port. Serves the UI and proxies /api/ to the API.
-      - "5173:8080"
+      # Loopback only. Upstream publishes a bare "5173:8080" -- i.e. 0.0.0.0,
+      # which would make this the one LAN-reachable service in the stack.
+      # SPOTTER serves this UI through its authenticating nginx gate at
+      # http://localhost:8082; the direct port stays bound to localhost only
+      # as a break-glass path.
+      - "127.0.0.1:5173:8080"
     volumes:
       # Override the baked-in nginx.conf to use system resolver (Podman-compatible).
       - ./flowsint-app/nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf:ro
